      "content": "Critics argue that standardized tests and IQ tests are inherently biased because they measure cultural capital, not innate ability. These tests are designed with a Eurocentric perspective, favoring the language, history, and values of the dominant culture. This cultural bias means that individuals from minority backgrounds, who may not share the same cultural references or educational experiences, are at a disadvantage. The tests don't account for diverse forms of intelligence or problem-solving skills that are developed outside of the traditional academic framework. As a result, they perpetuate a system that rewards those who are already privileged, rather than truly measuring merit. This is a clear example of how the supposed meritocracy is actually a facade that maintains the status quo and benefits the elite.",
